# id: M59-transaction-steps-batched-blind
# covering-test: TestSnapshotEquivalenceOracleReportsNothing
# package: ./sim/hunt/
# expect: killed
# power-seeds: 300
# power-floor: 130
# power-ceiling: 10
# power-measured: 273 of 300, first at seed 0, under current at commit 9c0c900+A6
# mutates: transaction steps in one Ready are staged into one batch and written once at the end, so a step cannot see the effects of the steps above it. Every step READS the engine before it writes -- a prewrite asks whether the key is locked, a resolve reads the lock and the primary's record -- so two prewrites of one key in one batch both succeed and the second overwrites the first's lock. Two transactions own one key and neither knows (BUG-018). The replica's state then depends on how many entries happened to arrive together, which is not a function of the log
